+## Failed session setup
+
+- If `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with that same error, provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model-response processing occurs after the failed setup, and cleanup receives the same session even when setup only partially completed, so deployers must track acquired resources and tolerate incomplete allocation rather than assume a turn finished ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
